    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="a853cfc3-31a2-5c71-b181-c4e9cf90c6fe" activityNameId="bc55a49d-9015-5bf8-9093-618423d226d4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, low voltage, consumer mix GO, at grid</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, low voltage, consumer mix GO, at grid
This dataset describes the transformation from medium to low voltage as well as the distribution of electricity at low voltage.; UUID:f98818a0-7b28-3b5c-8f43-9d2c250eb620
Included are the electricity production in Switzerland and from imports, the transmission network as well as direct SF6-emissions to air. Electricity losses during low-voltage transmission and transformation from medium-voltage are accounted for.
Location: Data apply to public and self producers. Geographical classification according to IEA. Transmission network, losses and emissions are taken from Itten, Frischknecht and Stucki (2014): LCI of Electricity Mixes and Grid.
Technology: Average technology used to distribute electricity. Includes underground and overhead lines, as well as air- and SF6-insulated medium-to-low voltage switching stations. Electricity production according to related datasets
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 
Sampling: Statistical data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f98818a0-7b28-3b5c-8f43-9d2c250eb620.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
